cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ephys_analysis"
abstract: >-
  A config-driven MATLAB pipeline for extracellular recordings: readers for
  Intan RHD, Open Ephys, TDT Synapse and a universal binary format; artifact
  screening; Kilosort4 sorting; derived LFP, MUA and spike-band signals;
  spike detection; Epsych2 behavior pairing; exports for Chronux, FieldTrip,
  kCSD-python and NWB; and quick-look analysis figures and reports.
authors:
  - family-names: Stolzberg
    given-names: Daniel
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/dstolz/ephys_analysis"
url: "https://github.com/dstolz/ephys_analysis/wiki"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - electrophysiology
  - extracellular recording
  - spike sorting
  - Kilosort4
  - MATLAB
  - Intan
  - Open Ephys
  - NWB
